# ============================================================================
# RAILWAY WORKER SERVICE CONFIGURATION
# ============================================================================
# This is NOT a separate Dockerfile - it's a reference document.
# Both backend and worker services use the SAME Dockerfile.railway
#
# SETUP IN RAILWAY:
# 1. Create TWO services from the same Dockerfile.railway:
#    - Service 1: "suna-backend" (API server)
#    - Service 2: "suna-worker" (Task queue)
#
# 2. For the WORKER service, override the start command:
#    Railway Dashboard → Service Settings → Deploy → Start Command:
#    uv run dramatiq --skip-logging --processes 4 --threads 4 run_agent_background
#
# 3. Environment variables needed for BOTH services:
#    - REDIS_HOST (Railway Redis service hostname)
#    - REDIS_PORT (Railway Redis service port)
#    - REDIS_PASSWORD (Railway Redis password)
#    - REDIS_SSL=True (Railway Redis uses SSL)
#    - All your Supabase/Auth/API keys
#
# WORKER SCALING RECOMMENDATIONS:
# - processes: Number of worker processes (4 = good for Railway's standard plan)
# - threads: Number of threads per process (4 = balanced)
# - Adjust based on your Railway plan's vCPU allocation
#
# Railway Resource Estimates:
# - Hobby Plan (0.5 vCPU): --processes 1 --threads 2
# - Pro Plan (2 vCPU): --processes 2 --threads 4
# - Pro+ Plan (4+ vCPU): --processes 4 --threads 4
# ============================================================================
